  "body": "```\r\ndata:text/html,<div%20style=\"cursor:%20pointer\"><button>ABC</button>%20DIV%20<label>DEF</label>%20DIV%20<select>GHI</select></div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nI don't see anything in the spec, but every browser behaves like that.\r\n\r\nIn Firefox, the specific rules are [this](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/b7f3977978922d44c7d92ae01c0d4cc2baca7bc2/layout/style/res/forms.css#76-78) for `label`, [this](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/b7f3977978922d44c7d92ae01c0d4cc2baca7bc2/layout/style/res/forms.css#230) for `select` and [this](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/b7f3977978922d44c7d92ae01c0d4cc2baca7bc2/layout/style/res/forms.css#97,546) for radio/checkbox and [this](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/b7f3977978922d44c7d92ae01c0d4cc2baca7bc2/layout/style/res/forms.css#599) for button and button-like inputs.\r\n\r\nIt seems it was done because we have a general `input { cursor: text }`. These days one would've probably used `cursor: inherit`, but unless there's any desire to change this which I doubt it, we should probably spec the current browser behavior.",
